  <Properties>
    <pitchId>
      <Value><![CDATA[_generic]]></Value>
    </pitchId>
    <cardsEpic>
      <Value><![CDATA[Make {project} global | Rollout to 40 markets. So far we have translated the cookie banner. That is all.
{project} 2.0 | Same as 1.0, but 'done properly this time'. Estimated in T-shirt sizes: tent.
The {project} platform | It is not a website any more. It is a platform. The price just doubled.
Digital transformation | Nobody can define it for {project}. Everyone agrees it is needed. Workshop on Thursday.
{project} for enterprise | Add single sign-on, an audit log and a PDF nobody reads. Triple the licence fee.
Migrate to the new Umbraco | Moving {project} 'should be straightforward'. Famous last words, now with a Gantt chart.]]></Value>
    </cardsEpic>
    <cardsStory>
      <Value><![CDATA[Remember me | As a user, I want {project} to remember me so that at least someone does after the julefrokost.
One more stakeholder | As a stakeholder who joined late, I want to question all of {project} so that I feel included.
The nephew's opinion | As the client's nephew, I want {project} in Comic Sans so that it 'pops'.
Estimate in peace | As a developer, I want to say '5 points' so that nobody replies 'but it is just a button'.
Export to Excel | As a finance user, I want to export {project} to Excel so that I never have to open it again.
Green status | As a PM, I want a green status for {project} so that I can go to lunch.
Bigger logo | As a client, I want the {project} logo bigger so that it can be seen from the motorway.
Works on their machine | As a developer, I want {project} to run on someone else's machine so that it is their problem.
Onboarding tour | As a new user, I want 14 tooltips in {project} so that I can close all 14 without reading.
Dark mode | As a designer, I want dark mode in {project} so that the bugs are harder to see.
Seasonal support | As a nisse, I want {project} to run in December only so that support can close for 11 months.
Go-live on a Friday | As a salesperson, I want {project} live on Friday at 16:00 so that I can promise it on Thursday.]]></Value>
    </cardsStory>
    <cardsFeature>
      <Value><![CDATA[Login | Users can log in to {project}. Logging out is phase 2.
Cookie banner | Covers 80% of {project}. The best-performing component we have.
Search | Finds nothing in {project}, very fast.
Newsletter popup | Appears after 0.3 seconds on {project}. The close button is 4 pixels wide.
Loading spinner | The most viewed screen in {project}. The designer is proud of it.
404 page | 'Oops!' and a sad nisse. The most creative work in all of {project}.
Share button | Share {project} on a network nobody has used since 2014.
Chatbot | Answers every question about {project} with 'Have you tried our FAQ?'
Hamburger menu | Hides the one link people actually need in {project}.
Carousel | Five slides on the {project} homepage. Nobody has ever seen slide 3.
Print stylesheet | For the one client who prints {project} and brings it to meetings.
Language switcher | EN / DA. Both show {project} in English.
Profile picture | Upload a photo to {project}. Maximum size: smaller than every photo you own.
Christmas mode | Snow falls over {project} from 1 December. So does performance.
Feedback form | Sends your thoughts about {project} to an inbox nobody owns.
Breadcrumbs | Home > {project} > Stuff > Other stuff > You are here (maybe).]]></Value>
    </cardsFeature>
    <cardsBug>
      <Value><![CDATA[Works in test, not in prod | {project} is fine on staging. Staging is fine. Staging is always fine.
Button does nothing | The big call to action in {project} has no click handler. Conversion is unchanged.
Fixed last sprint, back again | Same {project} bug, new ticket number. Its third anniversary is coming up.
Only fails for the client | {project} works for everyone except the one person who pays for it.
Headline says Lorem ipsum | Live on the {project} homepage since launch. Two people noticed. Both were us.
Crashes on 29 February | {project} cannot do leap years. The fix has been postponed to 2028. Twice.
Typo in the main headline | 'Welcom to {project}'. Approved by six people.
Cannot reproduce | A user says {project} 'feels weird'. No steps. No screenshot. Priority: critical.]]></Value>
    </cardsBug>
    <cardsTechdebt>
      <Value><![CDATA[TODO: fix before launch | Written in {project} in 2020. Launch was 2021. The TODO has seniority now.
helpers_new2.js | Everything in {project} imports it. Nobody knows what happened to helpers_new1.
Password in the README | The {project} admin login is 'admin / admin123'. It is also on a sticky note.
One test, and it is skipped | {project} has 0% coverage and a badge that says 'passing'.
The person who knows has left | All {project} documentation is a chat thread with someone who now works elsewhere.
Temporary workaround | Added to {project} 'just for the demo'. It is now the architecture.]]></Value>
    </cardsTechdebt>
    <cardsCeo>
      <Value><![CDATA[CEO Request: Can it also do AI? | '{project}, but with a little AI. Does not have to be much.' Said in the hallway, then gone.
CEO Request: Demo it on Friday | 'Just the happy path of {project}, for the board.' It is Thursday. There is no happy path.
CEO Request: An app version | '{project}, but in the App Store. How hard can it be?' Nobody answered. That was the answer.]]></Value>
    </cardsCeo>
    <siteHeroHeadline>
      <Value><![CDATA[{project}: finally, somebody built it.]]></Value>
    </siteHeroHeadline>
    <siteHeroSub>
      <Value><![CDATA[Nobody asked for {project}. The backlog said otherwise. Scoped in a hallway, estimated on a napkin, shipped on a Friday. What could go wrong?]]></Value>
    </siteHeroSub>
    <siteCta>
      <Value><![CDATA[Book a quick sync]]></Value>
    </siteCta>
    <sitePillars>
      <Value><![CDATA[Agile-ish | Built in two-week sprints that each took three. {project} is proof that velocity is a feeling.
Stakeholder approved | Signed off by the client, the client's boss and the client's nephew, who had notes on the logo.
Works on our machine | {project} runs flawlessly on one laptop in the office. So we ship the laptop.]]></Value>
    </sitePillars>
    <siteTestimonials>
      <Value><![CDATA[I don't know what {project} does, but the demo had confetti. Signed for three years.
It is not what we ordered. It is, however, exactly what we approved.
We asked for one small thing. It is on the roadmap. It has been on the roadmap since 2023.
My nephew could have built this. He didn't, though. So here we are.]]></Value>
    </siteTestimonials>
    <sitePricingJoke>
      <Value><![CDATA[Fixed price, then change requests. {project} Enterprise: call for a quote, and bring cake.]]></Value>
    </sitePricingJoke>
    <siteFooterLine>
      <Value><![CDATA[© {project}. All rights reserved, all estimates approximate. Built with love, coffee and one Friday deploy.]]></Value>
    </siteFooterLine>
